  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given here, threshold wavelength&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#197;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>550</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math></p><p>For photoelectric emission,&nbsp;the wavelength of the light should be less than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>550</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>.</p><p>Wavelength of infrared radiation&nbsp;extends from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>700</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>&nbsp;and that of ultraviolet radiation is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>.</p><p>Since, UV light has less wavelength than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>550</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>, so only UV would be able to emit photoelectrons.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
